+    <section id="why" class="block">
+      <div class="section-tag">The problem Braid is solving</div>
+      <h2 class="section-title">Your work should survive the model, machine, and session where it began.</h2>
+      <p class="copy">People increasingly use several AI systems: one for writing, another for research, another on a local workstation, and perhaps another at a different site. Each may be capable, but each usually begins with its own isolated context. Braid is a shared state layer for carrying forward the facts, constraints, decisions, observations, and relationships that should not have to be explained again from zero.</p>
+      <p class="copy" style="margin-top:16px"><strong style="color:var(--text)">One model can work alone. The moment you have two, continuity becomes infrastructure.</strong></p>
